35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My observations confirm a physical problem. There is significant congestion during the morning rush, with residents forced to move other bikes. Additionally, the rain exposure is uneven, making some spots far less desirable than others.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial situation is precarious. The ledger shows the account only covers basic maintenance; any significant changes requiring capital would need a levy. Also, the current cash collection already takes several hours of work monthly.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings confirm that the same flats have held the covered spaces for five years without any review. Furthermore, daily riders are actually willing to pay more for guaranteed access rather than treating every claim as equal.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we're dealing with a classic case of passive-aggressive tension. The complaint log shows people are annoyed but too timid to speak up, which is exactly how a toxic atmosphere begins.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that the treasurer already spends three hours a month just on cash! If we add more billing, it'll be a huge burden. Plus, people are already struggling to move bikes in the morning!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, your observation about the morning struggle aligns with mine. If we don't solve the physical congestion and the inequality of the rain-exposed spots, any new payment system will only add frustration to an already chaotic situation.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, while the physical layout is a problem, we must be realistic. Since the ledger shows we have no surplus, we cannot afford any infrastructure upgrades. Any solution must be self-sustaining and not require a levy on residents.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, I agree we must be realistic about costs. However, the fact that some residents have held the best spots for five years without review is a problem. We cannot ignore this perceived unfairness while discussing sustainability.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, you're focusing on ""fairness"" again. But look at the neighbors: a simple monthly charge turned residents into ghosts who avoid meetings. I'd rather have a few people with ""unfair"" spots than a building full of strangers.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, that sounds scary! But if the person managing the money gets totally burnt out, they'll become a ghost too! We need a system that's super simple so nobody hates their life doing the paperwork.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, avoiding conflict by ignoring the problem isn't a solution; it's just delaying the inevitable. We need a logical system that addresses the physical congestion and the disparity in spot quality to prevent further resentment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, logic dictates that a system is only as good as its implementation. If we create a complex tiered system to address spot quality, we increase the administrative burden on the treasurer, which @Mio already warned us about.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, simplicity is important, but so is legitimacy. If we simply maintain the status quo to save the treasurer's time, we are essentially endorsing a system of privilege that has lasted five years without oversight.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, ""legitimacy"" is a fancy word for creating a reason to fight. If we start auditing five years of habits, we're just inviting people to dig up old grudges. Let's prioritize peace over a perfect ledger.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, I get that it feels unfair, but digging up old grudges sounds like a lot of work! Let's find a way to be fair that doesn't make the manager's head explode from all the paperwork!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We must acknowledge that the current ""peace"" is an illusion if people are fighting over bikes every morning. A system that balances spot quality with a low administrative burden is the only logical path forward.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree that we need a balance. However, we must prioritize a system that requires zero capital investment and minimal administrative overhead. Any proposal that increases the treasurer's workload or requires a levy is logically unsustainable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"I believe we can achieve both. If we implement a system where those who value guaranteed access pay a fee, we address the unfairness of the status quo while potentially creating a fund for future maintenance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, you're dreaming of a gold mine, but you're ignoring the social cost. Charging for access creates a class system in the lobby. I've seen it happen next door; it turns neighbors into strangers. Let's keep it simple.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, I agree that keeping it simple is best! But ""simple"" should mean ""easy to manage,"" not just ignoring the problem. Let's pick the option that's the least stressful for everyone involved!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
